<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry Julius, Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1564–1613</span> · Also known as Henry Julius of Brunswick-Wolfenbüttel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry Julius, Duke of Brunswick-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luneburg">Lüneburg</a>, ruled the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolfenbuttel">Wolfenbüttel</a> from 1589 and was administrator of the Prince-Bishopric of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/halberstadt">Halberstadt</a> from 1566. A learned prince, he wrote plays, founded a court <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> and served as an adviser to Emperor Rudolf II in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a>. His tenure secured Halberstadt for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a> house and confirmed its Lutheran character.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-julius-duke-of-brunswick-luneburg.jpg" alt="Henry Julius, Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg" width="320" height="471" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dominicus Custos · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Heinrich_Julius_Braunschweig_MATEO.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
